    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d216">

                <pb facs="0405" n="277" sameAs="frus:frus1885/pg277"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">No. 216.</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Bayard to Mr.
                            Becerra</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1885-06-20"><hi rendition="#italic">June</hi> 20,
                        1885</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Acknowledging the receipt of your note of
                    the 18th instant, I have the honor to say that its statements concerning your
                    regret for the delayed action of the Colombian consul at New York, in the matter
                    of the brig Ambrose Light, have been made known to the Attorney-General.</p>
                <p>Accept, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>T. F. BAYARD.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
